      "ImageDescription": {
        "value": "Library (left) and Post Office (right) of the <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weedpatch_Camp\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Weedpatch Camp\">Weedpatch Camp</a></b> (also known as the Arvin Federal Government Camp and the Sunset Labor Camp) —  in outer <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Bakersfield,_California\" title=\"Category:Bakersfield, California\">Bakersfield</a>, southern <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:San_Joaquin_Valley\" title=\"Category:San Joaquin Valley\">San Joaquin Valley</a>, California.\n<ul><li>A 1930s <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Farm_Security_Administration\" title=\"Category:Farm Security Administration\">FSA—Farm Security Administration</a> project built by the <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Works_Progress_Administration\" title=\"Category:Works Progress Administration\">WPA—Works Progress Administration</a>.</li>\n<li>The plight of the Okies and a description of Weedpatch Camp were chronicled by novelist <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:John_Steinbeck\" title=\"Category:John Steinbeck\">John Steinbeck</a> in his book <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Grapes_of_Wrath\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:The Grapes of Wrath\">The Grapes of Wrath</a></i>.</li>\n<li>On the <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:National_Register_of_Historic_Places_in_Kern_County,_California\" title=\"Category:National Register of Historic Places in Kern County, California\">National Register of Historic Places in Kern County, California</a>.</li></ul>",
